Add an explicit "only act when asked" guard to the skill body

disable-model-invocation (Claude Code) and agents/openai.yaml (Codex)
are the harness-level manual-only mechanisms, but OpenCode confirmed
ignores the equivalent flag entirely (anomalyco/opencode#11972) and
Antigravity is unverified -- tracked in #12, neither fixable from this
fork. This is a pragmatic content-level mitigation: an explicit
instruction in the skill body itself, which every harness reads
regardless of whether it enforces manual-only invocation at the tool
level. It reduces the chance of unwanted output on a harness that
ignores the flag, but does not stop the skill from being loaded into
context there, and is a soft instruction a model could still ignore --
not a substitute for a real harness-level block.

